## Stated bounds (not silent gaps)

- Crash evidence lives in the owned durable window: the projector is
  read-only and owns no window of its own, so the secconftest points
  sit at the four `CreateSession` step boundaries (session-dir, record,
  events-dir, chain — one per boundary) and drive `Project`: faults at
  the first three derive the parked state with its exact retry, the
  identical retry heals into creating, and a fault past the chain
  derives creating with a session-exists refusal on retry. Purity pins
  idempotency on top (`TestReduceIsPure`,
  `TestProjectIsIdempotentAcrossReads`). No decorative points around
  reads were added (leaf 1's lesson).
- No `sessrepo` interface change needed: `Project` takes a session UUID
  and the listing distinguishes parked (entry present) from unknown
  (entry absent). `Resolve` still routes healthy sessions only — the
  sibling name-resolution leaf inherits that semantic unchanged.
- Out of scope by section: effective-profile derivation (§2.4),
  execution-realm readiness, workspace status, capability maps, sync age,
  peer names, interactive choice. Empty local host ID leaves the role
  unknown rather than guessing replica.
- Restatement is not a transition (documented derivation rule with its
  own test); unknown v1 types are inert by Section 5.2 with a dedicated
  test, and v2-v4 lifecycle types derive identically to v1 except the
  two v4 terminal/resume shapes.

## Notes for the reviewer

- Read `doc.go` first, then `sessstate.go` (`step`, `trackLease` →
  `successionMove`, `effect*`, `resolveWinner`), then `project.go`.
